49 683Q551 683 578 682T657 680Q684 680 713 681T746 682Q763 682 763 673Q763 669 760 657T755 643Q753 637 734 637Q662 632 617 587Q608 578 477 424L348 273L322 169Q295 62 295 57Q295 46 363 46Q379 46 384 45T390 35Q390 33 388 23Q384 6 382 4T366 1Q361 1 324 1T232 2Q170 2 138 2T102 1Q84 1 84 9Q84 14 87 24Q88 27 89 30T90 35T91 39T93 42T96 44T101 45T107 45T116 46T129 46Q168 47 180 50T198 63Q201 68 227 171L252 274L129 623Q128 624 127 625T125 627T122 629T118 631T113 633T105 634T96 635T83 636T66 637Z\"></path>\n</defs>\n<g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n <use xlink:href=\"#E3-MJMAIN-45\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E3-MJMAIN-5B\" x=\"681\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E3-MJMATHI-58\" x=\"960\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E3-MJMAIN-5D\" x=\"1812\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E3-MJMAIN-3D\" x=\"2368\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E3-MJMAIN-45\" x=\"3425\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E3-MJMAIN-5B\" x=\"4106\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E3-MJMAIN-45\" x=\"4385\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E3-MJMAIN-5B\" x=\"5066\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E3-MJMATHI-58\" x=\"5345\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E3-MJMAIN-2223\" x=\"6475\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E3-MJMATHI-59\" x=\"7031\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E3-MJMAIN-5D\" x=\"7795\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E3-MJMAIN-5D\" x=\"8073\" y=\"0\"></use>\n</g>\n</svg></span></p>\n<p>At first glance, this may look abstract, so let’s unpack what it means.</p>\n<p>The inner term <span class=\"mjpage\"><svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"8.567ex\" height=\"2.843ex\" style=\"vertical-align: -0.838ex;\" viewBox=\"0 -863.1 3688.6 1223.9\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-labelledby=\"MathJax-SVG-4-Title\">\n<title id=\"MathJax-SVG-4-Title\">\\textrm{E}[X \\mid Y]</title>\n<defs aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E4-MJMAIN-45\" d=\"M128 619Q121 626 117 628T101 631T58 634H25V680H597V676Q599 670 611 560T625 444V440H585V444Q584 447 582 465Q578 500 570 526T553 571T528 601T498 619T457 629T411 633T353 634Q266 634 251 633T233 622Q233 622 233 621Q232 619 232 497V376H286Q359 378 377 385Q413 401 416 469Q416 471 416 473V493H456V213H416V233Q415 268 408 288T383 317T349 328T297 330Q290 330 286 330H232V196V114Q232 57 237 52Q243 47 289 47H340H391Q428 47 452 50T505 62T552 92T584 146Q594 172 599 200T607 247T612 270V273H652V270Q651 267 632 137T610 3V0H25V46H58Q100 47 109 49T128 61V619Z\"></path>\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E4-MJMAIN-5B\" d=\"M118 -250V750H255V710H158V-210H255V-250H118Z\"></path>\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E4-MJMATHI-58\" d=\"M42 0H40Q26 0 26 11Q26 15 29 27Q33 41 36 43T55 46Q141 49 190 98Q200 108 306 224T411 342Q302 620 297 625Q288 636 234 637H206Q200 643 200 645T202 664Q206 677 212 683H226Q260 681 347 681Q380 681 408 681T453 682T473 682Q490 682 490 671Q490 670 488 658Q484 643 481 640T465 637Q434 634 411 620L488 426L541 485Q646 598 646 610Q646 628 622 635Q617 635 609 637Q594 637 594 648Q594 650 596 664Q600 677 606 683H618Q619 683 643 683T697 681T738 680Q828 680 837 683H845Q852 676 852 672Q850 647 840 637H824Q790 636 763 628T722 611T698 593L687 584Q687 585 592 480L505 384Q505 383 536 304T601 142T638 56Q648 47 699 46Q734 46 734 37Q734 35 732 23Q728 7 725 4T711 1Q708 1 678 1T589 2Q528 2 496 2T461 1Q444 1 444 10Q444 11 446 25Q448 35 450 39T455 44T464 46T480 47T506 54Q523 62 523 64Q522 64 476 181L429 299Q241 95 236 84Q232 76 232 72Q232 53 261 47Q262 47 267 47T273 46Q276 46 277 46T280 45T283 42T284 35Q284 26 282 19Q279 6 276 4T261 1Q258 1 243 1T201 2T142 2Q64 2 42 0Z\"></path>\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E4-MJMAIN-2223\" d=\"M139 -249H137Q125 -249 119 -235V251L120 737Q130 750 139 750Q152 750 159 735V-235Q151 -249 141 -249H139Z\"></path>\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E4-MJMATHI-59\" d=\"M66 637Q54 637 49 637T39 638T32 641T30 647T33 664T42 682Q44 683 56 683Q104 680 165 680Q288 680 306 683H316Q322 677 322 674T320 656Q316 643 310 637H298Q242 637 242 624Q242 619 292 477T343 333L346 336Q350 340 358 349T379 373T411 410T454 461Q546 568 561 587T577 618Q577 634 545 637Q528 637 528 647Q528 649 530 661Q533 676 535 679T549 683Q551 683 578 682T657 680Q684 680 713 681T746 682Q763 682 763 673Q763 669 760 657T755 643Q753 637 734 637Q662 632 617 587Q608 578 477 424L348 273L322 169Q295 62 295 57Q295 46 363 46Q379 46 384 45T390 35Q390 33 388 23Q384 6 382 4T366 1Q361 1 324 1T232 2Q170 2 138 2T102 1Q84 1 84 9Q84 14 87 24Q88 27 89 30T90 35T91 39T93 42T96 44T101 45T107 45T116 46T129 46Q168 47 180 50T198 63Q201 68 227 171L252 274L129 623Q128 624 127 625T125 627T122 629T118 631T113 633T105 634T96 635T83 636T66 637Z\"></path>\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E4-MJMAIN-5D\" d=\"M22 710V750H159V-250H22V-210H119V710H22Z\"></path>\n</defs>\n<g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n <use xlink:href=\"#E4-MJMAIN-45\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E4-MJMAIN-5B\" x=\"681\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E4-MJMATHI-58\" x=\"960\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E4-MJMAIN-2223\" x=\"2090\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E4-MJMATHI-59\" x=\"2646\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E4-MJMAIN-5D\" x=\"3410\" y=\"0\"></use>\n</g>\n</svg></span> is itself a <em>random variable</em>—its value depends on the outcome of <span class=\"mjpage\"><svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"2.42ex\" height=\"2.176ex\" style=\"vertical-align: -0.338ex;\" viewBox=\"0 -791.3 1042 936.9\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-labelledby=\"MathJax-SVG-5-Title\">\n<title id=\"MathJax-SVG-5-Title\">Y.</title>\n<defs aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E5-MJMATHI-59\" d=\"M66 637Q54 637 49 637T39 638T32 641T30 647T33 664T42 682Q44 683 56 683Q104 680 165 680Q288 680 306 683H316Q322 677 322 674T320 656Q316 643 310 637H298Q242 637 242 624Q242 619 292 477T343 333L346 336Q350 340 358 349T379 373T411 410T454 461Q546 568 561 587T577 618Q577 634 545 637Q528 637 528 647Q528 649 530 661Q533 676 535 679T549 683Q551 683 578 682T657 680Q684 680 713 681T746 682Q763 682 763 673Q763 669 760 657T755 643Q753 637 734 637Q662 632 617 587Q608 578 477 424L348 273L322 169Q295 62 295 57Q295 46 363 46Q379 46 384 45T390 35Q390 33 388 23Q384 6 382 4T366 1Q361 1 324 1T232 2Q170 2 138 2T102 1Q84 1 84 9Q84 14 87 24Q88 27 89 30T90 35T91 39T93 42T96 44T101 45T107 45T116 46T129 46Q168 47 180 50T198 63Q201 68 227 171L252 274L129 623Q128 624 127 625T125 627T122 629T118 631T113 633T105 634T96 635T83 636T66 637Z\"></path>\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E5-MJMAIN-2E\" d=\"M78 60Q78 84 95 102T138 120Q162 120 180 104T199 61Q199 36 182 18T139 0T96 17T78 60Z\"></path>\n</defs>\n<g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n <use xlink:href=\"#E5-MJMATHI-59\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E5-MJMAIN-2E\" x=\"763\" y=\"0\"></use>\n</g>\n</svg></span> The outer expectation then takes the average of that conditional expectation over all possible values of <span class=\"mjpage\"><svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"2.42ex\" height=\"2.176ex\" style=\"vertical-align: -0.338ex;\" viewBox=\"0 -791.3 1042 936.9\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-labelledby=\"MathJax-SVG-6-Title\">\n<title id=\"MathJax-SVG-6-Title\">Y.</title>\n<defs aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E6-MJMATHI-59\" d=\"M66 637Q54 637 49 637T39 638T32 641T30 647T33 664T42 682Q44 683 56 683Q104 680 165 680Q288 680 306 683H316Q322 677 322 674T320 656Q316 643 310 637H298Q242 637 242 624Q242 619 292 477T343 333L346 336Q350 340 358 349T379 373T411 410T454 461Q546 568 561 587T577 618Q577 634 545 637Q528 637 528 647Q528 649 530 661Q533 676 535 679T549 683Q551 683 578 682T657 680Q684 680 713 681T746 682Q763 682 763 673Q763 669 760 657T755 643Q753 637 734 637Q662 632 617 587Q608 578 477 424L348 273L322 169Q295 62 295 57Q295 46 363 46Q379 46 384 45T390 35Q390 33 388 23Q384 6 382 4T366 1Q361 1 324 1T232 2Q170 2 138 2T102 1Q84 1 84 9Q84 14 87 24Q88 27 89 30T90 35T91 39T93 42T96 44T101 45T107 45T116 46T129 46Q168 47 180 50T198 63Q201 68 227 171L252 274L129 623Q128 624 127 625T125 627T122 629T118 631T113 633T105 634T96 635T83 636T66 637Z\"></path>\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E6-MJMAIN-2E\" d=\"M78 60Q78 84 95 102T138 120Q162 120 180 104T199 61Q199 36 182 18T139 0T96 17T78 60Z\"></path>\n</defs>\n<g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n <use xlink:href=\"#E6-MJMATHI-59\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E6-MJMAIN-2E\" x=\"763\" y=\"0\"></use>\n</g>\n</svg></span></p>\n<p>In other words, we are averaging <span class=\"mjpage\"><svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"1.98ex\" height=\"2.176ex\" style=\"vertical-align: -0.338ex;\" viewBox=\"0 -791.3 852.5 936.9\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-labelledby=\"MathJax-SVG-7-Title\">\n<title id=\"MathJax-SVG-7-Title\">X</title>\n<defs aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E7-MJMATHI-58\" d=\"M42 0H40Q26 0 26 11Q26 15 29 27Q33 41 36 43T55 46Q141 49 190 98Q200 108 306 224T411 342Q302 620 297 625Q288 636 234 637H206Q200 643 200 645T202 664Q206 677 212 683H226Q260 681 347 681Q380 681 408 681T453 682T473 682Q490 682 490 671Q490 670 488 658Q484 643 481 640T465 637Q434 634 411 620L488 426L541 485Q646 598 646 610Q646 628 622 635Q617 635 609 637Q594 637 594 648Q594 650 596 664Q600 677 606 683H618Q619 683 643 683T697 681T738 680Q828 680 837 683H845Q852 676 852 672Q850 647 840 637H824Q790 636 763 628T722 611T698 593L687 584Q687 585 592 480L505 384Q505 383 536 304T601 142T638 56Q648 47 699 46Q734 46 734 37Q734 35 732 23Q728 7 725 4T711 1Q708 1 678 1T589 2Q528 2 496 2T461 1Q444 1 444 10Q444 11 446 25Q448 35 450 39T455 44T464 46T480 47T506 54Q523 62 523 64Q522 64 476 181L429 299Q241 95 236 84Q232 76 232 72Q232 53 261 47Q262 47 267 47T273 46Q276 46 277 46T280 45T283 42T284 35Q284 26 282 19Q279 6 276 4T261 1Q258 1 243 1T201 2T142 2Q64 2 42 0Z\"></path>\n</defs>\n<g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n <use xlink:href=\"#E7-MJMATHI-58\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\"></use>\n</g>\n</svg></span> in two stages:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>Within each scenario (for each possible value of <span class=\"mjpage\"><svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"1.773ex\" height=\"2.009ex\" style=\"vertical-align: -0.171ex;\" viewBox=\"0 -791.3 763.5 865.1\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-labelledby=\"MathJax-SVG-8-Title\">\n<title id=\"MathJax-SVG-8-Title\">Y</title>\n<defs aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E8-MJMATHI-59\" d=\"M66 637Q54 637 49 637T39 638T32 641T30 647T33 664T42 682Q44 683 56 683Q104 680 165 680Q288 680 306 683H316Q322 677 322 674T320 656Q316 643 310 637H298Q242 637 242 624Q242 619 292 477T343 333L346 336Q350 340 358 349T379 373T411 410T454 461Q546 568 561 587T577 618Q577 634 545 637Q528 637 528 647Q528 649 530 661Q533 676 535 679T549 683Q551 683 578 682T657 680Q684 680 713 681T746 682Q763 682 763 673Q763 669 760 657T755 643Q753 637 734 637Q662 632 617 587Q608 578 477 424L348 273L322 169Q295 62 295 57Q295 46 363 46Q379 46 384 45T390 35Q390 33 388 23Q384 6 382 4T366 1Q361 1 324 1T232 2Q170 2 138 2T102 1Q84 1 84 9Q84 14 87 24Q88 27 89 30T90 35T91 39T93 42T96 44T101 45T107 45T116 46T129 46Q168 47 180 50T198 63Q201 68 227 171L252 274L129 623Q128 624 127 625T125 627T122 629T118 631T113 633T105 634T96 635T83 636T66 637Z\"></path>\n</defs>\n<g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n <use xlink:href=\"#E8-MJMATHI-59\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\"></use>\n</g>\n</svg></span>), we find the expected value of <span class=\"mjpage\"><svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"2.627ex\" height=\"2.176ex\" style=\"vertical-align: -0.338ex;\" viewBox=\"0 -791.3 1131 936.9\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-labelledby=\"MathJax-SVG-9-Title\">\n<title id=\"MathJax-SVG-9-Title\">X.</title>\n<defs aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E9-MJMATHI-58\" d=\"M42 0H40Q26 0 26 11Q26 15 29 27Q33 41 36 43T55 46Q141 49 190 98Q200 108 306 224T411 342Q302 620 297 625Q288 636 234 637H206Q200 643 200 645T202 664Q206 677 212 683H226Q260 681 347 681Q380 681 408 681T453 682T473 682Q490 682 490 671Q490 670 488 658Q484 643 481 640T465 637Q434 634 411 620L488 426L541 485Q646 598 646 610Q646 628 622 635Q617 635 609 637Q594 637 594 648Q594 650 596 664Q600 677 606 683H618Q619 683 643 683T697 681T738 680Q828 680 837 683H845Q852 676 852 672Q850 647 840 637H824Q790 636 763 628T722 611T698 593L687 584Q687 585 592 480L505 384Q505 383 536 304T601 142T638 56Q648 47 699 46Q734 46 734 37Q734 35 732 23Q728 7 725 4T711 1Q708 1 678 1T589 2Q528 2 496 2T461 1Q444 1 444 10Q444 11 446 25Q448 35 450 39T455 44T464 46T480 47T506 54Q523 62 523 64Q522 64 476 181L429 299Q241 95 236 84Q232 76 232 72Q232 53 261 47Q262 47 267 47T273 46Q276 46 277 46T280 45T283 42T284 35Q284 26 282 19Q279 6 276 4T261 1Q258 1 243 1T201 2T142 2Q64 2 42 0Z\"></path>\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E9-MJMAIN-2E\" d=\"M78 60Q78 84 95 102T138 120Q162 120 180 104T199 61Q199 36 182 18T139 0T96 17T78 60Z\"></path>\n</defs>\n<g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n <use xlink:href=\"#E9-MJMATHI-58\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E9-MJMAIN-2E\" x=\"852\" y=\"0\"></use>\n</g>\n</svg></span></p>\n</li>\n<li><p>Across all scenarios, we take the weighted average of those conditional expectations, where the weights are the probabilities of each <span class=\"mjpage\"><svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"2.42ex\" height=\"2.176ex\" style=\"vertical-align: -0.338ex;\" viewBox=\"0 -791.3 1042 936.9\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-labelledby=\"MathJax-SVG-10-Title\">\n<title id=\"MathJax-SVG-10-Title\">Y.</title>\n<defs aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E10-MJMATHI-59\" d=\"M66 637Q54 637 49 637T39 638T32 641T30 647T33 664T42 682Q44 683 56 683Q104 680 165 680Q288 680 306 683H316Q322 677 322 674T320 656Q316 643 310 637H298Q242 637 242 624Q242 619 292 477T343 333L346 336Q350 340 358 349T379 373T411 410T454 461Q546 568 561 587T577 618Q577 634 545 637Q528 637 528 647Q528 649 530 661Q533 676 535 679T549 683Q551 683 578 682T657 680Q684 680 713 681T746 682Q763 682 763 673Q763 669 760 657T755 643Q753 637 734 637Q662 632 617 587Q608 578 477 424L348 273L322 169Q295 62 295 57Q295 46 363 46Q379 46 384 45T390 35Q390 33 388 23Q384 6 382 4T366 1Q361 1 324 1T232 2Q170 2 138 2T102 1Q84 1 84 9Q84 14 87 24Q88 27 89 30T90 35T91 39T93 42T96 44T101 45T107 45T116 46T129 46Q168 47 180 50T198 63Q201 68 227 171L252 274L129 623Q128 624 127 625T125 627T122 629T118 631T113 633T105 634T96 635T83 636T66 637Z\"></path>\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E10-MJMAIN-2E\" d=\"M78 60Q78 84 95 102T138 120Q162 120 180 104T199 61Q199 36 182 18T139 0T96 17T78 60Z\"></path>\n</defs>\n<g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n <use xlink:href=\"#E10-MJMATHI-59\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\"></use>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E10-MJMAIN-2E\" x=\"763\" y=\"0\"></use>\n</g>\n</svg></span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Let’s explore a few examples to build some intuition.</p>\n<!--We’ve seen that the law of total expectation allows us to compute the expectation of a random variable [math]X[/math] by conditioning on another variable [math]Y.[/math] This idea leads us to an even more powerful identity known as the **tower property**:\n\n\\[\n\\textrm{E}[X] = \\textrm{E}[\\textrm{E}[X \\mid Y]]\n\\]\n\nThis might look a bit abstract at first, so let’s break it down.\n\n\nThe inner term, [math]\\mathbb{E}[X \\mid Y],[/math] is itself a random variable because it depends on the value of [math]Y.[/math] The outer expectation then takes the average of that conditional expectation over all possible values of [math]Y.[/math]\n\nIntuitively, this means we're averaging [math]X[/math] in two steps:  \n\n* First, we compute the expected value of [math]X[/math] within each scenario defined by [math]Y.[/math]  \n\n* Then, we take the expected value of those conditional expectations, weighted by how likely each value of [math]Y[/math] is.\n\nLet’s explore a few examples to build some intuition.-->           \n                </div>        \n                    \n            </div>",
